#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless sea.
#> pause: 45
#> must: XXXX
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: pleasure dome
#> not: measureless
#> source: a\
# 8. d, n and a\: the paper's own example. McMahon 3.1
# n writes the current line (if it should be) and reads the next one in its
# place. a\ queues text to be appended after the line. d deletes the line and
# starts the next cycle at once: no later command runs on the corpse, but the
# queued XXXX is still written. So lines 1, 3, 5 appear, 2 and 4 become XXXX.
# Try: delete the n line. Now every line is replaced by XXXX. Why?
n
a\
XXXX
d

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
